*R Mac Plus compressed dispatch table.
*R The table contains 512 Toolbox entries followed by 256 OS entries.
*R Routine addresses are restored from the ROM and captured analysis.
*R The build assembles ROM-relative long offsets, then compresses them.
*R Zero entries become unimplemented-trap markers.
*R The macros retain the original trap-number and handler arguments.
*R See Evidence/dispatch-table.json for names, provenance, and encoding checks.

;
;	File:		DispTable.a
;
;	Copyright:	© 1986-1993 by Apple Computer, Inc., all rights reserved.
;
;	Change History (most recent first):

; Info:	This file builds the long version of the dispatch table based on values
;		calculated at link time.  In order to get a valid ROM image, a program
;		run post link time will compact the dispatch table and calculate the
;		new addresses.  Each table entry is either the value zero if it doesn't
;		exist, or the offset from ROMStart to the start of the routine.
;------------------------------------------------------------------------------


